BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8b5ccf0d05031a54@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Adult Education and Family Literacy 
 Week - September 13 through 19
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, thousands of adults in Maine need assistance to qu
 alify for better-paying or more fulfilling jobs\, to achieve a post-second
 ary education\, or to improve their English language skills\; and\nWHEREAS
 \n\, success in these endeavors leads to these adults becoming more effect
 ive family members\, citizens\, and workers\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine has o
 ver 65 adult education programs to assist residents seeking to become job-
 ready\, advance in the workplace\, prepare for a post-secondary education\
 , or increase their literacy in the English language\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, ad
 ult education can often provide this assistance in a more cost-effective m
 anner than other educational alternatives through a decentralized system t
 hat is within financial and geographic reach of anyone in the State of Mai
 ne\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, adult education students vary in age\, background\, 
 ethnicity\, and aspirations\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine is dedicated to helpi
 ng these students achieve the skills they need to expand their future care
 er and educational opportunities\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved tha
 t I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim
  the week of September 13-19\, 2026 as\nAdult Education and Family Literac
 y Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recogni
 ze this observance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal 
 of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this 
 twenty seventh day\nof August Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.go
 v/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-08-adult-education-
 and-family-literacy-week-september-13
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-adult-education-and-family-literacy-week-september-13
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ee66fea2fcec3af5@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Ovarian Cancer Awareness Month - Sep
 tember
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, ovarian cancer is the fifth leading cause of cance
 r deaths of women in the United States\, and it causes more deaths than an
 y other gynecologic cancer\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the American Cancer Society 
 estimates that 21\,010 cases of ovarian cancer will be newly diagnosed in 
 2026 and that 12\,450 individuals will die from the disease nationwide\, i
 ncluding 100 new cases and 70 deaths in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, many peop
 le are unaware of the symptoms of ovarian cancer\, which can often include
  bloating\, pelvic or abdominal pain\, difficulty eating or feeling full q
 uickly\, urinary issues\, and several more that are easily confused with o
 ther diseases\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the lack of an early detection test for o
 varian cancer combined with its vague symptoms means that approximately 80
  percent of cases of ovarian cancer are detected at an advanced stage\; an
 d\nWHEREAS\n\, all women are at risk for ovarian cancer\, but approximatel
 y 20 percent of women who are diagnosed with ovarian cancer have a heredit
 ary predisposition to the disease which places them at even higher risk\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, the family history of a woman has been found to play an i
 mportant role in accurately assessing their risk of developing ovarian can
 cer\, and medical experts believe that family history should be taken into
  consideration during the annual well-woman visit of any woman\; and\nWHER
 EAS\n\, ongoing investments in ovarian cancer research and education and a
 wareness efforts are critical to closing these gaps and improving survivor
 ship for women with ovarian cancer\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved tha
 t I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim
  September 2026 as\nOvarian Cancer Awareness Month\nthroughout the State o
 f Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testim
 ony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto a
 ffixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this twenty seventh\nof August Two 
 Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_document
 s/proclamations/2026-08-ovarian-cancer-awareness-month-september
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-ovarian-cancer-awareness-month-september
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c53cca3e4173a844@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] GEAR UP Week - September 21 through 
 25
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Gaining Early Awareness and Readiness for Undergra
 duate Programs (GEAR UP) is a federal grant program designed to increase t
 he number of low-income students who are prepared to enter and succeed in 
 postsecondary education and careers\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, GEAR UP Maine was f
 ounded in 1998\, and since then has helped prepare over 29\,000 students t
 o pursue education and career pathways they otherwise may not have been ab
 le to\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, administered by the University of Maine Farmingto
 n and the nonprofit Syntiro\, GEAR UP Maine supports students beginning in
  7th grade through high school and onward as they prepare for college\, ca
 reers\, and lifelong success\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, support provided by GEAR U
 P includes tutoring\, mentoring\, financial education\, college scholarshi
 ps\, career exploration\, and more\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, GEAR UP Maine will s
 erve 5\,000 students in seventh through twelfth grade during the current g
 rant period of 2023-2030\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine is committed to providin
 g a high-quality education for all students and helping them reach their h
 ighest potential\, no matter the path they choose\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, b
 e it resolved that I\, Janet Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do h
 ereby proclaim the week of September 21-25\, 2026 as\nGEAR UP Week\nthroug
 hout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this observ
 ance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State t
 o be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this twenty seventh
  day\nof August Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mil
 ls/official_documents/proclamations/2026-08-gear-week-september-21-through
 -25
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-gear-week-september-21-through-25
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4909f689ae78296c@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] National Hunting and Fishing Day - S
 eptember 26
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Maine has a rich and storied tradition of hunting 
 and angling that dates back further than the state itself and carries forw
 ard to this day\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, hunting and angling continue to be an i
 ntegral component of the cultural fabric of communities throughout the sta
 te\, and over recent years have offered a growing number of participants a
 n opportunity to connect with nature on a personal level while simultaneou
 sly providing food security\, a sense of self-sufficiency\, and both menta
 l and physical health benefits\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's sportsmen and wo
 men were among the first conservationists to support the establishment of 
 the Maine Department of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife to conserve fish\, w
 ildlife and their habitat\, and through their license fees helped fund sta
 te efforts to provide for healthy and sustainable natural resources\; and\
 nWHEREAS\n\, upon realizing that license fees alone were insufficient to r
 estore and sustain healthy fish and wildlife populations\, sportsmen and w
 omen supported self-imposed excise taxes on firearms and ammunition\, fish
 ing tackle and motorboat fuels to raise additional conservation funds\; an
 d\nWHEREAS\n\, to this day\, the Maine Department of Inland Fisheries and 
 Wildlife is funded\, in part\, by sportsmen and women\, through this Amer
 ican System of Conservation Funding – a “\nuser pays - public benefit
 s\n” approach that is widely recognized as the most successful model for
  funding fish and wildlife management in the world\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, last
  year alone\, Maine's sportsmen and women generated $32 million through th
 is system to support the conservation efforts of the Maine Department of I
 nland Fisheries and Wildlife\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 548\,194 hunters and angle
 rs support the state's economy through their spending\, contributing to th
 e $3.9 billion spent on outdoor activities in Maine last year\;\nNOW THERE
 FORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of
  Maine\, do hereby proclaim September 26\, 2026 as\nNational Hunting and \
 nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026
 -08-national-hunting-and-fishing-day-september-26
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-national-hunting-and-fishing-day-september-26
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fbe6a06e2b45ddd7@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T200223Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Deaf Culture Week - September 20 thr
 ough 26
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the United Nations\, the World Federation of the D
 eaf\, the National Association of the Deaf and 129 National Associations o
 f the Deaf throughout the world simultaneously participate in the Deaf Wor
 ld Week Celebration\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the State of Maine and its citizens
  observe the last full week of September as Deaf Culture Week in accordanc
 e with 1 MRSA § 132\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the statute recognizes the socioli
 nguistic community of Deaf people as a distinct group\, rich with its own 
 language\, traditions\, cultural values and norms\, history\, folklore\, l
 iterature and a network of organizations\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, American Sign 
 Language\, a visual-gestural language\, is recognized as the official stat
 e language of Deaf people\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, public schools and communitie
 s throughout the State are urged to observe Deaf Culture Week with appropr
 iate ceremony and cultural study\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, organizations\, repres
 entatives and friends of the Deaf community join in observing this signifi
 cant event in recognition of the Deaf community\, Deaf culture\, American 
 Sign Language and the celebration of the Deaf population\;\nNOW THEREFORE\
 n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Main
 e\, do hereby proclaim the week of September 20-26\, 2026 as\nDeaf Culture
  Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recogniz
 e this observance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal o
 f the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this t
 wentieth day\nof August Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/gove
 rnor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-08-deaf-culture-week-sept
 ember-20-through-26
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-deaf-culture-week-september-20-through-26
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:48183e296f0fb7a0@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T200223Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Safe Homes Awareness Month - Septemb
 er
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the 130th Maine Legislature unanimously passed L.D
 . 1861\, An Act to Establish the Safe Homes Program\, and as Governor\, I 
 signed the bill into law on April 7\, 2022\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, this biparti
 san law promotes the safe storage of prescription drugs\, firearms and oth
 er dangerous weapons in homes or public spaces\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the Safe
  Homes Program is an optional\, voluntary grant program that builds on the
  work of L.D. 1140\, An Act To Establish a Sales Tax Exemption for the Pur
 chase of Firearm Safety Devices\, by making storage devices\, such as gun 
 safes\, more affordable for people who want to buy them\; and\nWHEREAS\n\,
  the Safe Homes Program Fund will provide grants for purchasing safety dev
 ices for the safe storage of prescription drugs\, firearms\, and dangerous
  weapons in homes or public spaces\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, according to a repor
 t by the U.S. CDC\, there were 181 deaths by firearms in the State of Main
 e in 2024\, with over 86 percent of the deaths the result of suicide\; and
 \nWHEREAS\n\, in 2025\, there were 390 confirmed and suspected fatal drug 
 overdoses\, 20.4 percent lower than the total confirmed fatal overdoses fo
 r 2024\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, by ensuring that firearms and prescription drugs
  are properly stored and secured\, this law will reduce accidental gun dea
 ths\, prevent suicide\, and improve public health\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, in ac
 cordance with 1 MRSA § 150-R\, the month of September of each year is des
 ignated as Safe Homes Awareness Month to raise awareness of the importance
  of safety in the home and the assistance that is available through the Sa
 fe Homes Program established in Title 25\, section 7001\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE
 \n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Mai
 ne\, do hereby proclaim September 2026 as\nSafe Homes Awareness Month\nthr
 oughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this obs
 ervance\, promote the proper storage of prescription drugs and firearms\, 
 and learn more about the assistance available through the Safe Homes Progr
 am.\nI\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamatio
 ns/2026-08-safe-homes-awareness-month-september
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-safe-homes-awareness-month-september
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:04599e5aa206db87@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T200223Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Maine Honey Bee Day -  September 13
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, honey bees (Apis Mellifera) and other native insec
 ts are essential pollinators that contribute to food security by pollinati
 ng the plants we use and one-third of the food we consume\; and\nWHEREAS\n
 \, honey bees face serious threats from many sources including pests and v
 iruses\, loss of habitat\, toxic pesticide and herbicide usage\, and chang
 es in climate and resulting water patterns\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, honey bees a
 re essential in the production of Maine's heritage crops including blueber
 ries and apples\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's honey bees produce approximatel
 y 450\,000 pounds of honey each year and contribute an estimated annual $1
 00-150 million to the state’s economy\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine has almos
 t 2\,000 beekeepers ranging from hobbyists with as few as one hive\, to pa
 rt time business owners\, to full time commercial beekeepers with thousand
 s of hives\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, while traditional beekeeping occurred in rur
 al areas of Maine for the purpose of helping pollinate farm crops\, beekee
 ping is now growing in urban areas as the result of rising numbers of hobb
 y beekeepers interested in increasing biodiversity and local food producti
 on\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the State of Maine has an exemplary apiary inspectio
 n program for the protection of honey bees and education of beekeepers in 
 the prevention and spread of apiary diseases and pests\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 
 since 1975 the Honey Bee has been recognized as Maine's official state ins
 ect\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the Maine State Beekeepers Association is celebrati
 ng its 50th year of incorporation in 2026\, and will host the annual “Be
 e Fest” on September 13 at the Viles Arboretum in Augusta\;\nNOW THEREFO
 RE\n\, be it resolved\, that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of
  Maine do hereby proclaim September 13\, 2026 as\nMaine Honey Bee Day\nand
  I encourage all Maine people to join in recognizing the importance of hon
 ey bees to our state.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Sea
 l of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta thi
 s tw\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations
 /2026-08-maine-honey-bee-day-september-13
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-maine-honey-bee-day-september-13
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e2d0fa041a7a9f8e@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T200223Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Library Card Sign-up Month - Septemb
 er
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, libraries across the State of Maine are essential 
 to education\, imagination\, and opportunity\, providing early literacy pr
 ograms\, digital learning tools\, and lifelong pathways to knowledge and g
 rowth\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's libraries welcome all people\, serving as
  inclusive and accessible community spaces that connect individuals across
  cultures\, generations\, and life experiences\, and foster a strong sense
  of belonging\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's 257 public libraries reflect and 
 honor the diversity of Maine people\, honoring Wabanaki voices\, supportin
 g new Mainers\, preserving Franco-American heritage\, and uplifting rural\
 , coastal\, and urban communities alike through collections\, services and
  programs that are locally rooted\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, our libraries help Ma
 ine people navigate life's challenges by offering trusted information\, hi
 gh-speed internet\, job search and career support\, and vital connections 
 to health\, housing\, and social services – especially in communities wh
 ere other resources are limited or unavailable\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, our libr
 aries contribute to Maine's economic resilience by equipping workers\, stu
 dents\, entrepreneurs\, and small business owners with free access to trai
 ning\, online resources\, technology\, and other tools to succeed in this 
 changing world\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, through good times and bad\, Maine's lib
 rary staff have remained steadfast in their service – innovating\, adapt
 ing\, and going above and beyond to meet the evolving needs of their commu
 nities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, a library card opens doors for every Mainer – 
 to books and broadband\, to curiosity and creativity\, to ideas and inspir
 ation\, to lifelong learning and opportunity\, to the local and global com
 munity\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Gov
 ernor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim September 2026 as\nLibrar
 y Card Sign-up Month\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I encourage all 
 Mainers to sign up for a library card and explore the many resources\, pro
 grams\, and opportu\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_document
 s/proclamations/2026-08-library-card-sign-month-september
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-library-card-sign-month-september
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fee31cadf6567aa1@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260824T185810Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260824
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] 10th Anniversary of the Katahdin Woo
 ds and Waters National Monument - August 24
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, on August 24\, 2016\, the eve of the National Park
  Service’s 100th anniversary\, President Barack Obama officially designa
 ted 87\,500 acres of Maine’s North Woods as the Katahdin Woods and Water
 s National Monument\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, for thousands of years\, this land 
 has been home to Wabanaki people who traversed the Penobscot’s waterways
  and negotiated the deep woods in search of food\, furs\, medicines and ot
 her resources\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, countless others have come to know the be
 auty and serenity of this land that native peoples had already known for c
 enturies – those like Henry David Thoreau\, Theodore Roosevelt and Perci
 val Baxter – who helped share this special place with the world and comm
 anded us to preserve it\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, this land has also been vital t
 o generations of Maine people who make their living by logging and working
  in the forest products industry\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the establishment of t
 he monument would not have been possible without the lifelong dedication o
 f Roxanne Quimby and her family to preserve this precious piece of Maine\,
  along with the conservationists\, philanthropists\, and advocates who con
 tinue supporting it\, including the Friends of Katahdin Woods & Waters\; a
 nd\nWHEREAS\n\, since its creation\, the monument has greatly benefited ne
 ighboring communities as visitors from in and out of Maine travel to exper
 ience its beauty\, and in 2024 alone\, visitors spent $2.7 million in loca
 l communities near the park\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, with the Katahdin Woods and
  Waters Monument\, we have safeguarded this place that has meant so much t
 o so many people\, ensuring that everyone can come camp\, hike\, fish\, ta
 ke in a night sky\, or just enjoy nature in its purest form for generation
 s to come\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Go
 vernor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim August 24\, 2026 as the\
 n10th Anniversary of the Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument\nand 
 I urge everyone to visit the monument\, embrace the raw beauty of Maine\, 
 and do th\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclama
 tions/2026-08-10th-anniversary-katahdin-woods-and-waters-national
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-10th-anniversary-katahdin-woods-and-waters-national
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:add1f6965716269d@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260820T185634Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Maine Blood Donation Day - September
  4
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the State of Maine is committed to ensuring the sa
 fety and security of all those living in and visiting our state\; and\nWHE
 REAS\n\, a sufficient blood supply is a public health issue both locally a
 nd nationally\, and our hospitals and medical centers need a readily avail
 able supply for our residents and visitors\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, one blood do
 nation can help save more than one life\, and although most of the U.S. po
 pulation is eligible to donate blood\, only about 3 percent actually do\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine is home to many organizations committed to raising 
 awareness about the importance of blood donation\, including the American 
 Red Cross\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine Blood Donation Day effectively serves t
 o remind us that we need to constantly replenish our blood supply through 
 donation and community awareness\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that 
 I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim S
 eptember 4th\, 2026 as\nMaine Blood Donation Day\nthroughout the State of 
 Maine\, and I urge all Maine people to support our local blood drives as s
 aving lives and protecting our residents is our primary goal.\nIn testimon
 y whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto aff
 ixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this seventeenth day\nof August Two T
 housand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents
 /proclamations/2026-08-maine-blood-donation-day-september-4
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-maine-blood-donation-day-september-4
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d65f25883d921c60@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260820T185634Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] National Clean Energy Week - Septemb
 er 15 through 19
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\,\nMaine is committed to advancing an affordable\, rel
 iable\, and cleaner energy future and enjoys abundant forms of renewable e
 nergy that power homes and businesses across the State\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nc
 lean energy sources including solar\, wind\, hydropower\, and biomass faci
 lities provide cost-effective power to Maine and the region\; and\nWHEREAS
 \,\nthe generation of power from renewable sources\, including forms such 
 as hydro\, wood\, wind\, and solar\, accounts for\n54 percent of net elect
 ricity generation in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nMaine has increased its Renew
 able Portfolio Standard to 90 percent by 2040 and adopted a complementary 
 Clean Energy Standard to reach 100 percent clean energy by 2040\; and\nWHE
 REAS\,\nMaine leads New England in wind-powered generation\, and ranks el
 eventh in the country in its share of electricity generated from wind\; an
 d\nWHEREAS\,\nin 2024\, hydroelectric power generated nearly 20 percent o
 f the electricity in Maine\, and Maine ranked ninth in the nation for hydr
 opower production as a share of total energy generated\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nM
 aine’s more than 16\,000 clean energy jobs grow local economies and boo
 st economic development\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nMaine has led the nation in the 
 adoption of high efficiency electric heat pumps\, installing more than 200
 \,000 units with a goal of 275\,000 installed by 2027\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nNa
 tional Clean Energy Week provides an opportunity for individuals\, local g
 overnments\, corporations\, and other organizations in Maine to champion c
 ommonsense solutions that address the United States’ evolving economic a
 nd energy needs\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\,\nbe it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mil
 ls\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim September 15-19\,
  2026\, as\nNational Clean Energy Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\, an
 d I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testimony whereof\
 , I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN
  under my\nhand at Augusta this seventeenth day of\nAugust Two Thousand Tw
 enty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamat
 ions/2026-08-national-clean-energy-week-september-15-through-19
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-national-clean-energy-week-september-15-through-19
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dfbf69209c839f65@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260820T185634Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Direct Support Professionals Recogni
 tion Week - September 13 through 19
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Direct Support Professionals (DSPs) are the primar
 y providers of community-based long-term support services for thousands of
  individuals with disabilities in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, DSPs are valued
  for their work in building respectful and trusted relationships with indi
 viduals to assist them with their most intimate needs\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, D
 SPs provide essential support that ensures that individuals with disabilit
 ies are included as a valued part of their community\; supported at home\,
  at work\, and in communities across Maine\; and empowered to live with th
 e dignity that all people of our state deserve\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, DSPs pro
 vide a broad range of individualized supports\, including meal preparation
 \, medication assistance\, personal care and life skills training\, mobili
 ty\, work and life enrichment opportunities\, and other daily tasks\; and\
 nWHEREAS\n\, DSPs support informed choices and person-centered practices t
 hat honor and respect the individuals with disabilities that they serve\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, an adequate workforce of high-quality DSPs is necessary f
 or the people of Maine to respond to the needs of people with disabilities
 \, and to avoid more costly institutional care\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be i
 t resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do h
 ereby proclaim the week of September 13-19\, 2026 as\nDirect Support Profe
 ssionals Recognition Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all 
 citizens to recognize these individuals who provide vital support and care
  for older adults\, people with intellectual disabilities\, autism spectru
 m disorder and other related conditions and help them live full and meanin
 gful lives in their community.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe 
 Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Au
 gusta this seventeenth day\nof August Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.
 maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-08-direct-s
 upport-professionals-recognition-week-september-13
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-direct-support-professionals-recognition-week-september-13
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fa0457a31fa7e332@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260820T185634Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] 30th Anniversary of the Maine Intern
 ational Trade Center - August 18
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, in 1996\, Governor Angus S. King\, Jr. and a unani
 mous Maine Legislature established the Maine International Trade Center as
  a public-private partnership\, merging existing state trade-development e
 fforts together to support Maine businesses and strengthen Maine’s econo
 my through international commerce\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, for three decades\, t
 he Maine International Trade Center has adapted to sweeping changes in tec
 hnology\, global markets\, and trade policy while remaining a trusted\, no
 npartisan international economic development partner\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, th
 e Maine International Trade Center has become Maine’s leading source for
  international business assistance\, providing customized consulting\, mar
 ket intelligence\, technical assistance\, funding\, education\, and worldw
 ide connections to exporters and importers of every size in all 16 countie
 s\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the Maine International Trade Center has worked with 
 thousands of clients and facilitated approximately $350 million in export 
 sales\, helping Maine products\, services\, and innovations reach customer
 s around the world while supporting jobs and economic opportunity in rural
 \, coastal\, and urban communities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, trade missions led b
 y the Maine International Trade Center have carried Maine businesses from 
 neighboring Canadian provinces to markets across Europe\, Asia\, Latin Ame
 rica\, and beyond\, while international delegations and partnerships have 
 brought new relationships\, ideas\, and opportunities home to Maine\; and\
 nWHEREAS\n\, in 2016\, the United States Department of Commerce honored th
 e Maine International Trade Center with the President’s “E” Award\, 
 the nation’s highest recognition for significant contributions to the ex
 pansion of United States exports\, and its Future Global Leaders program h
 as provided practical international business experience to more than 200 i
 nterns\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the Maine International Trade Center’s success
  reflects the dedication of its staff\, board members\, business members\,
  public of\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclam
 ations/2026-08-30th-anniversary-maine-international-trade-center-august
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-30th-anniversary-maine-international-trade-center-august
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a2c4ffb576989488@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260716T033355Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Maine Commercial Fishing Remembrance
  Day - July 21
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the State of Maine has long been shaped by the pro
 ud and enduring traditions of our working waterfronts\, where generations 
 have built their lives and livelihoods on the sea\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, comme
 rcial fishing remains one of Maine’s most iconic and economically vital 
 industries\, supporting thousands of hardworking men and women and contrib
 uting significantly to coastal communities and the state’s heritage\, ec
 onomy\, and way of life\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the risks faced by Maine’s fi
 shermen are real and constant\, with unpredictable weather\, treacherous w
 aters\, and the physical demands of the job posing dangers each day they s
 et out to sea\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, too many have made the ultimate sacrifice
  in the pursuit of their work\, and Maine communities continue to bear the
  deep and lasting sorrow of lives lost to the sea\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, July 
 21\, 2026 shall serve as a solemn day of remembrance for those we have los
 t\, a time to honor their lives and contributions\, and to extend our deep
 est condolences to their families\, friends\, and fellow fishermen\; and\n
 WHEREAS\n\, on this day\, Maine organizations that support fishing communi
 ties have come together in a call to action – to renew our shared commit
 ment to improving safety and recovery in the commercial fishing industry\,
  strengthening training\, resources\, equipment\, and awareness to protect
  those who continue to work on the water\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, through rememb
 rance and responsibility\, we honor the past\, safeguard the present\, and
  ensure a more secure future for all Maine fishermen\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\
 , be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\
 , do hereby proclaim July 21\, 2026 as\nMaine Commercial Fishing Remembran
 ce Day\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to pause i
 n honor of our fallen fishermen\, to support the commercial fishing commun
 ity\, and to recommit to promoting a culture of safety and wellness on and
  off the water.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused the Great Seal of th
 e State to \nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/procla
 mations/2026-07-maine-commercial-fishing-remembrance-day-july-21
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-maine-commercial-fishing-remembrance-day-july-21
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1d12b9acfdbd9071@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260707T151201Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Maine Community Health Center Week -
  August 2 through 8
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, for nearly 60 years\, Maine’s community health c
 enters have provided high-quality\, affordable\, comprehensive primary and
  preventive health care in our rural and underserved communities\; and\nWH
 EREAS\n\, as Maine's largest primary care network\, community health cente
 rs are the health care home for over 210\,000 Maine people\; and\nWHEREAS\
 n\, Maine's community health centers are leaders in fighting the chronic d
 isease epidemic by expanding access to primary care\, which keeps people h
 ealthy and out of expensive settings like hospital emergency rooms\; and\n
 WHEREAS\n\, Maine's community health centers develop new approaches to int
 egrating a wide range of services beyond primary care\, including nutritio
 n\, oral health\, vision\, behavioral health\, and pharmacy services\, to 
 provide comprehensive care that allows each patient to thrive\; and\nWHERE
 AS\n\, Maine's community health centers are governed by patient-majority b
 oards\, ensuring patients are engaged in their health care decisions\; and
 \nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's community health centers are locally owned and opera
 ted small businesses that serve as critical economic engines\, helping to 
 power local communities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's community health center
 s are on the front lines of emerging health care crises\, providing access
  to care for 10 percent of Maine's veterans\, addressing the opioid epidem
 ic\, and responding to public health threats\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Community 
 Health Center Week offers the opportunity to celebrate Maine's community h
 ealth center organizations with more than 100 service delivery sites in al
 l 16 Maine counties\, and we honor their dedicated staff\, board members\,
  patients\, and all those responsible for their continued success and grow
 th since the first community health centers opened their doors over 60 yea
 rs ago\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Gov
 ernor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim the week of August 2-8\, 
 2026\, as\nMaine Community Health Center Week\nand I encourage all residen
 ts to\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamation
 s/2026-07-maine-community-health-center-week-august-2-through-8
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-maine-community-health-center-week-august-2-through-8
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:867077455de5ecce@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260707T151201Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Wild Blueberry Weekend - August 1 an
 d 2
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, wild blueberries (Vaccinium angustifolium) emerged
  on the rocky\, acidic soils of the barrens of Maine following the retreat
  of the glaciers more than 10\,000 years ago\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, wild blueb
 erries\, which are not planted but grow naturally\, were first managed and
  harvested by the Wabanaki and are now grown by 512 Maine farms on approxi
 mately 40\,000 acres\, within Cumberland\, Franklin\, Hancock\, Lincoln\, 
 Kennebec\, Knox\, Penobscot\, Piscataquis\, Waldo\, and Washington countie
 s\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine produces nearly 100 percent of all wild blueber
 ries in the United States\, and they are one of the top three specialty cr
 ops produced in the state\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine's wild blueberry grower
 s and businesses are significant contributors to Maine's economy and are v
 ital to Maine's rural communities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, wild blueberries can 
 be enjoyed fresh during the height of summer in Maine\, while Individual Q
 uick Freezing (IQF) technology allows consumers to buy berries frozen at t
 he peak of freshness all year round\, all over the world\; and\nWHEREAS\n\
 , Maine wild blueberries are one of the world's top 10 superfoods\, a deep
  blue fruit that is rich in antioxidants and health benefits\; and\nWHEREA
 S\n\, wild blueberries are recognized as Maine's official state berry\; an
 d blueberry pie is recognized as the official state dessert\; and\nWHEREAS
 \n\, the Wild Blueberry Commission of Maine is\, in this year of 2026\, or
 ganizing the sixth annual Wild Blueberry Weekend to encourage residents an
 d visitors to visit wild blueberry farms and participating establishments 
 and eat\, drink\, and experience the state's iconic fruit and the landscap
 e where wild blueberries grow\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I
 \, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim th
 e first weekend of August – August 1-2\, 2026 as\nWild Blueberry Weekend
 \nin Maine\, and I encourage all people to recognize the vital contributio
 ns made by the state's wild blueberry growers and businesses to our econom
 y\, and t\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclama
 tions/2026-07-wild-blueberry-weekend-august-1-and-2
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-wild-blueberry-weekend-august-1-and-2
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8eba6cd9503c96c3@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260707T151201Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Maine Korean War Veteran Recognition
  Day - July 27
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, on June 27\, 1950\, in response to the communist t
 hreat to South Koreans and their democracy\, President Harry S. Truman com
 mitted the first United States forces to combat in South Korea\, beginning
  the Korean War\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, nearly 1.8 million members of the Unite
 d States Armed Forces served alongside the forces of the Republic of Korea
  and 20 other Allied nations under the United Nations Command to defend fr
 eedom and democracy on the Korean Peninsula\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the Korean 
 War was one of the bloodiest wars in history\, with 36\,574 American death
 s\, approximately 103\,284 wounded\, and 8\,157 listed as missing-in-actio
 n\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, seventy-three years have passed since the signing of 
 the cease-fire agreement at Panmunjom on July 27\, 1953\, yet the Korean p
 eninsula still technically remains in a state of war\, and the Korean War 
 has become a “Forgotten War” to many Americans\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the 
 State of Maine recognizes the service and bravery of all Korean War vetera
 ns\, and we remember the 242 Maine people who lost their lives for our nat
 ion during the Korean War\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, in accordance with 1 MRSA § 
 150\, the State of Maine designates July 27th of each year as Maine Korean
  War Veteran Recognition Day\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\
 , Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim Jul
 y 27\, 2026 as\nMaine Korean War Veteran Recognition Day\nthroughout the S
 tate of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn 
 testimony whereof\, I have caused the Great Seal of the State to be hereun
 to affixed GIVEN under my hand at Augusta this sixth day of July Two Thous
 and Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/pro
 clamations/2026-07-maine-korean-war-veteran-recognition-day-july-27
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-maine-korean-war-veteran-recognition-day-july-27
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:554d2d45e3e66293@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260707T151201Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Wyeth Day - July 12
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Maine has provided inspiration for much of the bod
 y of work produced by the Wyeth family starting in 1930\, when N.C. Wyeth 
 purchased a summer home in Port Clyde and he built a small studio\; and\nW
 HEREAS\n\, while N.C. Wyeth was best known for his illustrations\, many of
  which were derived from his Maine-based knowledge of coastal and maritime
  life\, he was also an acclaimed painter\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, son of N.C. Wy
 eth and one of the United States’ most celebrated realist painters of th
 e 20th century\, Andrew Wyeth’s detailed paintings depict the land\, sea
 \, and people well known to him\, including the work he is most well-known
  for\, Christina’s World\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Betsy Wyeth\, wife of Andrew
  and mother of Jamie\, helped establish the Wyeth Center at the Farnsworth
  Art Museum and played a key role in founding the Island Institute\, an or
 ganization devoted to sustaining Maine’s coastal and island communities\
 ; and\nWHEREAS\n\, a painter like his father and grandfather before him\, 
 Jamie Wyeth’s paintings of everyday life can be found in the collections
  of the Farnsworth Art Museum\, the National Gallery of Art\, the National
  Portrait Gallery\, the Museum of Modern Art\, the Fine Arts Museum of San
  Francisco\, and many others\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, while members of the Wyeth
  family are known to the world for their generations of fine art\, to many
  Mainers they have been best known as neighbors and friends\; and\nWHEREAS
 \n\, in accordance with 1 MRSA §150-D\, the state of Maine designates Jul
 y 12th\, Andrew Wyeth’s birthday\, as Wyeth Day in recognition of the fa
 mily’s contributions to the State’s artistic and cultural heritage\;\n
 NOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of t
 he State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim July 12\, 2026 as\nWyeth Day\nthrou
 ghout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this obser
 vance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused the Great Seal of the State 
 to be hereunto affixed GIVEN under my hand at Augusta this sixth day of
  July Two Thousand Twe\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_docum
 ents/proclamations/2026-07-wyeth-day-july-12
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-wyeth-day-july-12
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3aa4b32c719badf4@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260704T191745Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260702
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] America's Semiquincentennial - July 4
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, on July 4\, 1776\, the Continental Congress adopte
 d the Declaration of Independence\, asserting the United States’ indepen
 dence from Great Britain and setting forth a defining promise of liberty\,
  equality\, and self-government\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, July 4\, 2026\, marks t
 he 250th anniversary of that historic declaration\, known as America’s S
 emiquincentennial\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the American experiment rests on the 
 enduring principle that power rests with the people – not a king – and
  that liberty is secured through democratic self-government and the rule o
 f law\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, for 250 years\, Americans have sustained that pro
 mise through free and fair elections\, the peaceful transfer of power\, re
 spect for constitutional limits\, and a shared commitment to the instituti
 ons of our democracy\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, while the founding promise of libe
 rty and equality was imperfectly realized at our nation’s birth\, genera
 tions of Maine people and Americans have worked to extend those ideals and
  their benefits more fully to all\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine people\, then c
 itizens of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts\, played an early\, consequen
 tial role in the fight for American independence\, including Kittery nativ
 e William Whipple\, the only native Mainer to sign the Declaration of Inde
 pendence\, and the patriots at Machias who captured the British armed cutt
 er Margaretta\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, on June 21\, 1775\, soon after the Battle
  of Bunker Hill\, Penobscot Chief Joseph Orono met with General George Was
 hington at Watertown and agreed that his tribe’s warriors\, as well as o
 thers in the Wabanaki Confederacy\, would join forces with the Continental
  Army to fight a common enemy in the struggle for freedom\; and\nWHEREAS\n
 \, on October 18\, 1775\, British warships shelled and burned Falmouth\, n
 ow Portland\, in retaliation for its resistance to the Crown\, an attack t
 hat strengthened the resolve of Maine people in support of independence\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, the sacrifices of Maine people during the Revolutionary W
 ar helped secur\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/pr
 oclamations/2026-07-americas-semiquincentennial-july-4
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-07-americas-semiquincentennial-july-4
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a77003411b20d4d5@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260701T202235Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] 211 Maine Day - July 7
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, 211 Maine is a Maine-based health and human servic
 es and emergency preparedness and response helpline\, providing free and c
 onfidential referrals to needed resources to Maine people\; and\nWHEREAS\n
 \, 211 Maine provides 24/7 service statewide by people employed in Maine t
 hrough efficient and effective response to the growing complexities and ne
 eds of Maine residents\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, for 20 years\, 211 Maine has wor
 ked diligently to confront and reduce the stigma associated with seeking s
 upport by affirming that doing so reflects personal strength\; and\nWHEREA
 S\n\, since 2006\, 211 Maine specialists have answered more than 1 million
  calls from people across the state looking for needed information from ho
 using support and food resources to substance use and recovery services\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, 211 Maine provides emergency operations support during ti
 mes of natural and other disasters\, including assisting the Maine Emergen
 cy Management Agency field calls from those impacted and collecting data t
 o inform severity and locations of need\, and directing people looking for
  local heating shelters or cooling centers\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 211 Maine ha
 ndles several specialized services and partnerships\, including providing 
 the Opiate Helpline and the Gambling Helpline\, distributing emergency hea
 ting assistance through the Keep Me Warm fund\, and serving as a resource 
 for mental health services and tax preparation\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, 211 Main
 e stands as a compelling example of how coordinated efforts among governme
 nt\, nonprofit organizations\, and private-sector partners can elevate the
  well-being of Maine's citizens\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I
 \, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim Ju
 ly 7\, 2026 as\n211 Maine Day\nthroughout the state\, and I urge everyone 
 to utilize and spread awareness of this important resource for Maine peopl
 e.\nthe Great Seal of the State to be hereunto affixed GIVEN under my hand
  at Augusta this twenty fifth day of June Two Thousand Twenty-\nhttp://www
 .maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-06-211-mai
 ne-day-july-7
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-06-211-maine-day-july-7
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4ff19205563342b6@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260701T202235Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260623
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Saint Jean-Baptiste Day - June 24
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Maine enjoys a large\, vibrant Franco-American com
 munity\, largely as a result of French Canadians immigrating to the state 
 between 1840 and 1930\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, at least twenty-five percent of M
 aine citizens claim Franco-American heritage\, and French is the second-mo
 st spoken language in the state\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nthe significant cultural
 \, economic\, and civic contributions made by Franco-Americans have enrich
 ed the culture and lives of Maine people\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine benefits
  from a close and prosperous relationship with its Canadian neighbors\, an
 d despite uncertain federal policy Maine will always welcome our Canadian 
 friends to visit our state\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the feast of Saint Jean the 
 Baptist is an important French cultural observance\, celebrated in America
  as early as 1636\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, in accordance with 1 MRSA § 120\, th
 e State of Maine and its citizens observe June 24th as Saint Jean-Baptiste
  Day\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governo
 r of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim June 24\, 2026 as\nSaint Jean
 -Baptiste Day\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to 
 recognize this observance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused the Great
  Seal of the State to be hereunto affixed GIVEN under my hand at Augusta t
 his seventeenth day of June Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/
 governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-06-saint-jean-baptist
 e-day-june-24
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-06-saint-jean-baptiste-day-june-24
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f73dac11f1838643@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260701T202235Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260616
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] James Weldon Johnson Day - June 17
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, An Act To Create a James Weldon Johnson Annual Obs
 ervance Day and an Observance Task Force was enacted in Maine on June 20\,
  2021\, to honor the life and perpetuate the legacy of one of our nation
 ’s great Civil Rights leaders\, that of the author\, educator\, journali
 st\, lawyer\, and diplomat James Weldon Johnson\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, this pr
 olific member of the Harlem Renaissance made significant contributions to 
 the preservation and development of African American cultural heritage thr
 ough his poetry\, fiction\, autobiography\, anthologies\, and in collabora
 tion with his brother\, J. Rosamund Johnson\, wrote over 200 songs for Bro
 adway as well as “Lift Every Voice and Sing\,” widely considered to be
  the Black national anthem\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, James Weldon Johnson broke m
 any barriers as the first African American admitted to the Florida Bar\, t
 he first African American Field Director and Executive Secretary of the Na
 tional Association for the Advancement of Colored People\, and the first A
 frican American to serve as U.S. Consul to Venezuela and Nicaragua\; and\n
 WHEREAS\n\, James Weldon Johnson found solace from the endless struggle fo
 r racial justice and his extraordinarily active life among the pines and r
 ocky shores of Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, it was following a tragic accident
  that took place in Wiscasset\, Maine on June 26\, 1938 that this Jacksonv
 ille\, Florida native succumbed to his injuries\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, observi
 ng James Weldon Johnson Day encourages Mainers to learn more about both Ja
 mes Weldon Johnson and our state’s history\, including the many contribu
 tions of African Americans dating back to before statehood\; and\nWHEREAS\
 n\, in accordance with 1 MRSA § 150-Q\, June 17th of each year is designa
 ted as James Weldon Johnson Day in honor of writer and civil rights activi
 st James Weldon Johnson\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Jan
 et T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim June 17\
 , 2026 as\nJames Weldon Johnson Day\nin Maine\, and I urge all citizens to
  observe t\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclam
 ations/2026-06-james-weldon-johnson-day-june-17
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-06-james-weldon-johnson-day-june-17
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:84db92b0b9eb5644@gov-executive-orders.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260701T202235Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260616
SUMMARY:[Governor / Executive Branch] Native American Veterans Day - June 
 21
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, on June 21\, 1775\, soon after the Battle of Bunke
 r Hill in the early stages of the American Revolution\, Penobscot Chief Jo
 seph Orono met with General George Washington at Watertown and agreed that
  his tribe’s warriors\, as well as others in the Wabanaki Confederacy\, 
 would join forces with the Continental Army to fight a common enemy in the
  struggle for freedom\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, members of 33 tribes served as co
 de talkers in World War I and World War II\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, more than 44
 \,000 Native Americans served with distinction between 1941 and 1945\, inc
 luding members of Maine’s Penobscot\, Passamaquoddy\, Maliseet\, and Mi'
 kmaq tribes\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Native American men and women on the home f
 ront were also an integral part of the WWII effort\, with more than 40\,00
 0 leaving their communities to work in ordnance depots\, factories\, and o
 ther war industries\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Native Americans invested more than
  $50 million in war bonds and contributed to the Red Cross and the Army an
 d Navy Relief societies\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Native American women served in
  the Army Nurse Corps during WWI\, and nearly 800 Native American women se
 rved with units such as the Army Corps\, the Army Nurse Corps\, and the WA
 VES throughout the duration of WWII\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Native American men
  and women\, including those from Maine\, have continued to serve in the a
 rmed forces in every war since\, including Korea\, Vietnam\, Desert Storm\
 , Afghanistan\, and Iraq\, and in current operations to enhance the securi
 ty of American partners around the world\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, in accordance 
 with 1 MRSA § 150-C\, the State of Maine and its citizens observe June 21
 st as Native American Veterans Day in remembrance of the courage and dedic
 ated service of Native American members of the United States Armed Forces\
 ;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor o
 f the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim June 21st\, 2026 as\nNative Amer
 ican Veterans Day\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens
  to recognize\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proc
 lamations/2026-06-native-american-veterans-day-june-21
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-06-native-american-veterans-day-june-21
CATEGORIES:Governor / Executive Branch
